{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1157758-interesting-observations-on-subjective-reality","id":1157758,"title":"Interesting observations on subjective reality","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-11-11T08:27:29-08:00","id":1157758,"title":"Interesting observations on subjective reality","content":"So, it does have a biased political opinion in various parts, but look past that for now, please, and look hard at the parts about personal reality. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.theatlantic.com/magazine/archive/2017/09/how-america-lost-its-mind/534231/?utm_source=atlfb\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.theatlantic.com/magazine...m_source=atlfb</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-02T20:39:31-08:00","id":1164731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Article</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">From the start, our ultra-individualism was attached to epic dreams, sometimes epic fantasies\u2014every American one of God\u2019s chosen people building a custom-made utopia, all of us free to reinvent ourselves by imagination and will.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now I can't get a Mage-version of <i>I'm Afraid of Americans</i> out of my head.<br /> <br /> &quot;Johnny wants a node, Johnny wants to enchant his coat. Johnny wants an acolyte, Johnny wants to think of a rote...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T01:43:35-08:00","id":1164745,"title":"","content":"So, every mage might as well be a nascent Marauder? Cool to work with, but not sure if desirable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-03T21:08:59-08:00","id":1164962,"title":"","content":"The current American culture seems less than ideal for the Technocracy, but not really great for the Traditions either. Part of this cultural shift is a backlash against universalism. Since the the Traditions existence depends on very different cultures getting along, this is bad news for them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T05:52:10-08:00","id":1165023,"title":"","content":"This article is a fascinating in the meta-narrative it is trying to lure us in to accepting. On the surface how well it works depends a great deal on how much you accept that the author knows what he is talking about. That's true of a lot of articles, really, but most of them invite us to look at the facts and agree or disagree accordingly. Because of this its storytelling nature and flow, this article invites us to disagree about our perceptions. It invites us to say, &quot;well that's not how I remember it...&quot; or &quot;that's not how I understood it...&quot; both of which are appeals to differing mental pictures of the world. In disagreeing with the article, we accept it's core premise.<br /> <br /> He really should have kept the politics out of it, though, because those are the sections that actually invited me to question his facts and knowledge rather than his perceptions. But in one sense that makes this article even better inspiration for Mage. It could be a textbook example for how Mages try to influence sleeper ideas, both in the way it presents an idea and in the way it breaks down.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-04T10:10:03-08:00","id":1165087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1157758-interesting-observations-on-subjective-reality?p=1165023#post1165023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He really should have kept the politics out of it, though, because those are the sections that actually invited me to question his facts and knowledge rather than his perceptions. But in one sense that makes this article even better inspiration for Mage. It could be a textbook example for how Mages try to influence sleeper ideas, both in the way it presents an idea and in the way it breaks down.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but would the article even been published if not for the current climate of &quot;fake news&quot; and &quot;alternative facts&quot;?<br /> <br /> See, it just keeps going! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}